@page "/help"
@layout MainLayout

<PageTitle>User Guide - IntelliMed</PageTitle>

<h4 class="mb-1">User Guide</h4>
<p class="text-muted small mb-4">Step-by-step walkthroughs for common tasks in IntelliMed.</p>

<div class="card mb-3">
    <div class="card-header"><strong>The Patient Visit, Start to Finish</strong></div>
    <div class="card-body">
        <p class="text-muted small">From booking through to checkout — what to click, and when.</p>

        <div class="list-group list-group-flush">

            <div class="list-group-item border-start border-3 border-primary ps-3">
                <span class="badge bg-secondary me-1">1</span> <strong>Booking</strong>
                <span class="badge bg-light text-dark border ms-1">Reception</span>
                <p class="mb-0 mt-1 small">
                    Book via <strong>New Appointment</strong> or the <strong>Calendar View</strong> — pick the client, practitioner, date and time.
                    Starts as <span class="badge bg-secondary">Scheduled</span>.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="list-group-item border-start border-3 border-primary ps-3">
                <span class="badge bg-secondary me-1">2</span> <strong>Confirm</strong>
                <span class="text-muted small">— optional</span>
                <span class="badge bg-light text-dark border ms-1">Reception</span>
                <p class="mb-0 mt-1 small">
                    If you call ahead to confirm the booking, open the appointment's <strong>Details</strong> panel and click <strong>Confirm</strong>.
                    Skipping this doesn't block anything later.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="list-group-item border-start border-3 border-primary ps-3">
                <span class="badge bg-secondary me-1">3</span> <strong>Check-in</strong>
                <span class="badge bg-light text-dark border ms-1">Reception</span>
                <p class="mb-0 mt-1 small">
                    When the patient arrives, open <strong>Details</strong> and click <strong>Mark Arrived</strong>.
                    They now appear in the <a href="/appointments/waiting-room">Waiting Room</a> list.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="list-group-item border-start border-3 border-success ps-3">
                <span class="badge bg-secondary me-1">4</span> <strong>Doctor / Nurse Calls Them In</strong>
                <span class="badge bg-light text-dark border ms-1">Doctor / Nurse</span>
                <p class="mb-0 mt-1 small">
                    From the Waiting Room, click <strong>Start</strong> — or click <strong>Progress Note</strong> to do the same thing and open the note in one step.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="list-group-item border-start border-3 border-success ps-3">
                <span class="badge bg-secondary me-1">5</span> <strong>The Consult</strong>
                <span class="badge bg-light text-dark border ms-1">Doctor / Nurse</span>
                <p class="mb-0 mt-1 small">
                    Document Reason for Visit, then Subjective / Objective / Assessment / Plan. Part of an ongoing issue?
                    Tag the note to an <strong>Episode</strong> — pick an existing one or start a new one right there.
                    Prescribe something during the visit and it's <strong>logged into the note automatically</strong> the moment it's issued.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="list-group-item border-start border-3 border-success ps-3">
                <span class="badge bg-secondary me-1">6</span> <strong>Finalize the Note</strong>
                <span class="badge bg-light text-dark border ms-1">Doctor / Nurse</span>
                <p class="mb-0 mt-1 small">
                    Click <strong>Finalize &amp; Sign</strong>. The note locks — later corrections are added as a dated addendum, never an edit to
                    what was originally written. Tick the box to also mark the appointment <span class="badge bg-success">Completed</span> in the same click.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="list-group-item border-start border-3 border-primary ps-3">
                <span class="badge bg-secondary me-1">7</span> <strong>Checkout / Billing</strong>
                <span class="badge bg-light text-dark border ms-1">Reception</span>
                <p class="mb-0 mt-1 small">
                    Once the visit is <span class="badge bg-success">Completed</span>, a <strong>New Invoice</strong> button appears right on the
                    appointment — already linked to the client and the visit.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="list-group-item border-start border-3 border-primary ps-3">
                <span class="badge bg-secondary me-1">8</span> <strong>Payment</strong>
                <span class="badge bg-light text-dark border ms-1">Reception</span>
                <p class="mb-0 mt-1 small">
                    The invoice screen has a "record payment now" option — cash, EFTPOS, etc. Take it on the spot, or leave the invoice open
                    if the patient is claiming through a health fund.
                </p>
            </div>

            <div class="list-group-item ps-3">
                <span class="badge bg-success me-1"><i class="bi bi-check-lg"></i></span> <strong>Patient Leaves</strong>
                <p class="mb-0 mt-1 small">
                    Everything from this visit — timestamps, the signed note, prescriptions, the invoice, the payment — stays linked to this
                    one appointment for good.
                </p>
            </div>

        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="card mb-3">
    <div class="card-header"><strong><i class="bi bi-signpost-split me-1"></i>Walk-ins (No Prior Booking)</strong></div>
    <div class="card-body">
        <p class="text-muted small">The Waiting Room only lists appointments booked in advance, so there's no check-in step there for a walk-in. Here's the actual flow:</p>

        <ol class="small ps-3 mb-3">
            <li class="mb-2"><strong>Find or create the patient</strong> — <strong>Find Client</strong>, search for them. Brand new patient? Create the client record first, same as normal.</li>
            <li class="mb-2"><strong>Open Progress Notes &rarr; + New</strong> — on the client's record, not through the Waiting Room.</li>
            <li class="mb-2"><strong>Nothing is created yet</strong> — the editor opens empty. Leave without saving and nothing is left behind.</li>
            <li class="mb-2">
                <strong>First save creates the appointment</strong> — the moment <strong>Save Draft</strong> or <strong>Finalize &amp; Sign</strong> is
                clicked for the first time, IntelliMed creates a same-day appointment (dated today, starting now), immediately marks it
                <span class="badge bg-primary">InProgress</span>, and links the note to it. From here it's a real appointment like any other.
            </li>
            <li><strong>Everything after that is identical to a booked visit</strong> — consult, prescribing, Finalize &amp; Sign, checkout, payment.</li>
        </ol>

        <div class="alert alert-warning small py-2 mb-2">
            <i class="bi bi-exclamation-triangle me-1"></i>
            <strong>Double-check the Practitioner field before that first save.</strong> The auto-created appointment is attributed to
            whichever practitioner is selected at that moment — changing it on the note afterward does <em>not</em> update the appointment.
        </div>

        <div class="alert alert-secondary small py-2 mb-0">
            <i class="bi bi-info-circle me-1"></i>
            If a patient has a booking later today but walks in early for something unrelated, use this same <strong>+ New</strong> path —
            it creates a second, separate appointment for the walk-in.
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="card">
    <div class="card-header"><strong>Appointment Status Badges</strong></div>
    <div class="card-body">
        <p class="text-muted small">These colours appear throughout the app on every appointment.</p>
        <table class="table table-sm align-middle mb-0">
            <tbody>
                <tr><td style="width:160px"><span class="badge bg-secondary">Scheduled</span></td><td class="small text-muted">Booked, awaiting the visit</td></tr>
                <tr><td><span class="badge bg-info text-dark">Confirmed</span></td><td class="small text-muted">Booking confirmed with the patient</td></tr>
                <tr><td><span class="badge bg-warning text-dark">Arrived</span></td><td class="small text-muted">Checked in, waiting to be seen</td></tr>
                <tr><td><span class="badge bg-primary">InProgress</span></td><td class="small text-muted">Currently with the doctor/nurse</td></tr>
                <tr><td><span class="badge bg-success">Completed</span></td><td class="small text-muted">Visit finished, ready to invoice</td></tr>
                <tr><td><span class="badge bg-dark">Cancelled</span></td><td class="small text-muted">Booking cancelled before the visit happened</td></tr>
                <tr><td><span class="badge bg-danger">NoShow</span></td><td class="small text-muted">Patient didn't attend</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</div>
